On Mon, Jun 9, 2014 at 3:21 AM, Gleki Arxokuna <gleki.is.my.name@gmail.com>
wrote:

>
>>
>> canja/cerda/cirko/cnemu/dirba/dunda/friti/jdima/jerna/jinga/kargu/pleji/prali/vamji/vecnu
>>
>> There are other words that involve possession/transfer/exchange but for
>> which the gismu list doesn't say anything explicitly about "sumti-raising",
>> for example:
>> claxu/pindi/ricfu/punji/sabji/jmina/dejni/jarco/lebna/cpacu/jbera/cuxna/vimcu/cpedu/mipri/sisku/sarji
>> /cupra/dirce/ferti/xaksu/tisna/daspo/ralte
>>
>> It's a non-problem for me to correct {dunda}. The main obstacle for me is
> that there might be much more than those 15 brivla that would allow
> "object" => "property" change.
>

Indeed. I already listed 24 more.

In my version of gimste all those places are marked as "located" and ... in
> fact the majority of places are "located" throughout the gimste.
>

 It is to be expected that the majority of places will be first and
foremost for concrete objects. I think the biggest problem will be for
those who are very anti-metaphor, or anti-unmarked metaphor, because they
need to know exactly when a place admits a property in a literal sense and
when it doesn't. For example, if I say "lo ka ce'u jbopre cu pagbu mi", is
that literal or metaphoric? What about "lo ka ce'u senpi cu pagbu lo ka
ce'u remna"? The official gismu list doesn't specify any types for "pagbu".
What about "lo ka ce'u jbopre cu panlo mi"?

mu'o mi'e xorxes

